    <SU_Hint>The Profit and Loss with Previous Year Comparison Report is a local currency report that lists the selected accounting period, current year to date, same period last year and last year to date balances of general ledger revenue and cost accounts.  This report summarises profit movement within the selected accounting period in comparison with same period last year and documents the financial returns resulting from all business activity and overhead expenditure. 

The report can be filtered by Accounting period, Department and Branch.  By default the report only lists those accounts with financial activity. When running this report, you can also choose to include all general ledger accounts, including those with no transactions.

